":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115312","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115312","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115312.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115312.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"- Follow-up to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/88349.\r\n\r\nThe texture types AtlasTexture, CanvasTexture and MeshTexture are only supported in a 2D context.\r\n\r\nThis hides them from the inspector to avoid confusion, but you can still set them explicitly in a script if desired. This way, backwards compatibility is preserved. (I'll handle the `.expected` file changes ASAP, it doesn't change the actual exposed API.)\r\n\r\nI'm unsure if CameraTexture and ExternalTexture are supported in 3D contexts, e.g. to be displayed on a material or sky texture. I couldn't get either to work locally, even in 2D. cc @BastiaanOlij\r\n\r\n- See https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/1708,\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/33855,\r\nand https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107367.\r\n\r\n## Preview\r\n\r\nBefore | After\r\n-|-\r\n<img width=\"290\" height=\"695\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a7d718d6-d4c4-40f2-b04d-a0d6c35c20c4\" /> | <img width=\"290\" height=\"624\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b387e2bf-7b1c-40f8-b9f0-b957cf9df719\" />\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115312/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115312/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}